        "Pinned real algebraic source: TauCeti.ModelTheory.Algebra.OrderedRing.MvPolynomial.",
        H("Pinned real algebraic source: TauCeti.ModelTheory.Algebra.OrderedRing.MvPolynomial."),
        Blocks(Paragraph(Text("This content adaptation retains selected declarations and proof bodies from TauCetiProject/TauCeti revision 1f9b4414105d86e487a4ac4c3d3397076a44d0d2, TauCeti/ModelTheory/Algebra/OrderedRing/MvPolynomial.lean. The D5 import paths connect its actual proof dependencies to the original cone boundary consumer. It does not assume a cylindrical decomposition or semialgebraic projection certificate. The original source ownership is retained and no independent escape credit is claimed. Full license and attribution appear in the Lean source and docs/reports/licenses/TauCeti-LICENSE.txt. Each adaptation is retired when the actual pinned mathlib supplies an equivalent statement, replacing consumers by direct applications of that owner.")),
        Paragraph(Text("For arbitrary types α and β, the compiler sends a variable a to X a and the ordered-ring term constructors +, multiplication, negation, zero and one to the corresponding integer-polynomial operations. The order-language summand has no function symbols. Over every commutative ring R with Ring.CompatibleRing R and the original order-language structure, realize_eq_aeval_toMvPolynomial identifies realization at v : α → R with aeval v of the compiled polynomial. Its recursion uses exactly the compatibility equations at the actual operands. The surjectivity proof constructs terms for integer constants, sums and multiplication by a variable; exists_term_realize_eq_eval assigns coefficient parameters to Sum.inl and original variables to Sum.inr.")),
        Paragraph(Text("For every t and g : α → β, compilation of t.relabel g equals rename g of its compilation. Instantiate realization to MvPolynomial β ℤ with its usual ring compatibility and any order-language structure; apply pinned FirstOrder.Language.Term.realize_relabel, MvPolynomial.aeval_X_left_apply and rename_eq_aeval. The integer algebra map agrees with the coefficient inclusion by uniqueness of a ring homomorphism from ℤ; this identifies the aeval identity with the actual coefficient ring instance. No preservation of an order by rename is required. These are identities for every term and valuation, not only closed terms. The useful formula translation uses realize_eq_eval_map_toMvPolynomial on both equality operands and both order operands, retaining the original QF and quantifier-elimination telescopes.")))));
